185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 121 0 R
/E (The recent macroeconomic scenario was marked by an accelerated pace of events, including the geopolitical effects of Donald Trump's election in the US and a negative supply shock that drove up agricultural commodity prices in late 2024 and early 2025. This international scenario increased uncertainty and impacted the Brazilian economy, primarily through the exchange rate. Despite the challenges, IPEA \(Institute for Applied Economic Research\) projected a 2.2% growth for the Brazilian economy in 2025. Although export performance was similar in the first half of 2025 compared to 2024, partial data for the second half of 2025 point to growth, indicating that the economy is expected to continue expanding.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
